n coaching high school football for six years.","published":"2026-11-19T12:19:43.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50514617/philip-rivers-nc-state-fairhope-alabama","type":"Story","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 12 Game Day Kickoff: Appreciating Jeremiah Smith's greatness","description":"What to expect in Week 12, from top games and players to teams on upset alert.","published":"2026-11-19T17:08:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/page/gamedaykickoff111926/week-12-top-games-upsets-preview","type":"Story","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Inside the complexities of clock management in college football","description":"From Michigan-WMU to Notre Dame-BYU, the closing seconds of games seem to be more puzzling than ever.","published":"2026-11-19T12:17:18.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522229/the-complexities-clock-management-college-football","type":"Story","byline":"Ryan McGee","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5114314/taylor-wein","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taylor_Wein"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Taylor Wein","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taylor_Wein","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:23Z","intro":"Taylor Wein is an American college football defensive lineman for the Oklahoma Sooners.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Wein attended Nolensville High School in Nolensville, Tennessee. As a senior, he totaled 91 tackles, 31 tackles for loss, 13 sacks, and four forced fumbles. A four-star recruit, Wein committed to play college football at the University of Oklahoma."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Wein redshirted in 2023 and played sparingly in 2024, totaling two tackles. His production significantly increased in 2025, having a breakout season while becoming a starter on the Sooners' defensive line. Against South Carolina, Wein recorded four tackles, two tackles for loss, and his first career interception. Against No. 4 Alabama, he totaled three tackles, a sack, and forced fumble, while also blocking a field goal in a 23–21 victory."}]}}